SonarQube
SonarQube is a code quality and security analysis platform widely used in DevOps and CI/CD pipelines.
What it does
It performs static code analysis to find issues without running the code:
🐞 Bugs (logic errors)
🔐 Security vulnerabilities
⚠️ Code smells (maintainability issues)
📊 Code coverage & duplication
📐 Technical debt
Why it’s important in DevOps
Acts as a quality gate before code is merged or deployed
Prevents bad or insecure code from reaching production
Encourages clean, maintainable code across teams
How to Setup SonarQube?
Step 1: Java is mandatory to install Sonarqube
Step 2: To download and rename the sonarqube 
-->cd /opt
-->sudo wget https://lnkd.in/dK79nktS
-->sudo unzip sonarqube-10.4.1.88267.zip
-->sudo mv sonarqube-10.4.1.88267 sonarqube
Step 3: Create SonarQube user and give permissions
-->sudo adduser sonarqube
-->sudo chown -R sonarqube:sonarqube /opt/sonarqube
-->chmod -R 775 /opt/sonarqube
Step 4: Configure system limits (MANDATORY)
-->Here go inside file /etc/sysctl.conf for that use the command sudo nano /etc/sysctl.conf and then add the following line “vm.max_map_count=262144” and then apply the same for that use command sudo sysctl -p
-->After that Edit the limits: for that go inside file sudo nano /etc/security/limits.conf and Add below lines and save the file and get out from the file
sonarqube  -  nofile  65536
sonarqube  -  nproc   4096
Step 5: Switch to sonarqube user and start
-->sudo su – sonarqube here we will switch to the sonarqube user
-->/opt/sonarqube/bin/linux-x86-64/sonar.sh start By running this command sonarqube will get start
This is how our Sonarqube will get configure successfully!!!
Step 6: Access SonarQube By using EC2-instance’s public ip:9000 as below
http://public ip:9000, Port 9000 is the default port of the Sonarqube.
